{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB13257 - MONDO_1245",
  "verbalization": "Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous is associated with Microcytic Anemia through a chain of indications that ultimately point to iron deficiency, a key driver of microcytic anemia. The evidence suggests that Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous is used to treat Iron Deficiency Anemia, which in turn is linked to Ferumoxytol and Ferric Maltol, both of which are indicated for Microcytic Anemia. This pathway highlights the role of iron deficiency in the pathophysiology of microcytic anemia, with Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous serving as a primary treatment for iron deficiency. The integration of these indications supports the notion that Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous may be repurposed for the treatment of Microcytic Anemia, particularly in cases of iron deficiency. The mechanism is supported by the recurring theme of iron deficiency as a central factor in the development of microcytic anemia, with Ferrous Sulfate Anhydrous acting as a key therapeutic agent in this context.",
